<section vertical-align="center">
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item>
      <h2>Freedom takes institutional form</h2>
      <p>Freedom is not simply doing whatever one wants. It takes shape through practices and institutions in which individual agency and shared norms can support one another.</p>
      <grid divider="3pt palette-2" vertical-sizing="hug">
        <grid-item colspan="20">
          <p role="eyebrow">Person</p>
          <h3>Individual agency</h3>
          <p>I form purposes, make commitments, and act.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20">
          <p role="eyebrow">Practice</p>
          <h3>Shared norms</h3>
          <p>Speaking, listening, challenge, and responsibility make agency effective.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item colspan="20">
          <p role="eyebrow">Institution</p>
          <h3>Durable social form</h3>
          <p>Roles, rights, procedures, and avenues for revision organize freedom over time.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <aside variant="caution">
        <p><b>No automatic progress.</b> Hegel interprets history through conflicts within forms of social life. Institutions can embody freedom inadequately, expose contradictions, and remain open to criticism and change.</p>
      </aside>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>